(* Compare — ARO-0001, GitLab #469
 *
 * Compare reads BOTH operands and binds a fresh result. The older
 * two-operand spelling tried to rebind its own first operand and could never
 * run under immutability.
 *
 * `<r: matches>` is the boolean; `<r: result>` is equal / less / greater.
 *)

(Application-Start: Comparisons) {
    Create the <expected> with 10.
    Create the <actual> with 10.
    Create the <smaller> with 3.
    Create the <bigger> with 42.

    Compare the <same> from the <expected> against the <actual>.
    Log "equal: ${<same: matches>} / ${<same: result>}" to the <console>.

    Compare the <above> from the <expected> against the <smaller>.
    Log "greater: ${<above: matches>} / ${<above: result>}" to the <console>.

    Compare the <below> from the <expected> against the <bigger>.
    Log "less: ${<below: matches>} / ${<below: result>}" to the <console>.

    (* Strings compare too, and the result drives an ordinary guard. *)
    Create the <role> with "admin".
    Compare the <is-admin> from the <role> against "admin".
    Log "admin access" to the <console> when <is-admin: matches>.

    Return an <OK: status> for the <startup>.
}
